# EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR: (13,25): The elements of a collection literal are not boxed: this one is Int, and a Vector<IntRef> holds IntRef
# EXPECT_ERROR_COUNT: 1
#~
A collection literal is the array its Vector is constructed from, and the elements of an
array are not boxed one by one: numbers for a Vector<IntRef> are refused at the first
number, with the ways to write it (the holders, an IntVector, or AddBack, which boxes).
One error, not the constructor's error about an Int[].
~#
use Collection;

class BadCollectionLiteralUnboxed {
	function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
		v : Vector<IntRef> := [1, 2, 3];
		v->Size()->PrintLine();
	}
}
